ay","a":"—","d":"","n":"#311","p":13,"im":["a5d081a64aba419975c88e0dda6b94b7c7ec070c","d9e9ec9bec538e3a47f234f97f5a9c729c1a258f"],"m":311},{"id":"flaglimits_p13_312","t":"Aaron\n\nHi Scott,\n\nGood charting.\n\nI have attached a few charts that may give you some things to think about, not saying they're correct though, just my 10 pips\n\nI understand where you have marked the FTR area on the 1st chart, so I will jump to the second chart what I see, is the lowest zone is an FTR, above this is an SR flip where as you pointed out, price reacted well at this price level. I agree the next green level is a DP point to engulf, the engulf is\n\n1707\n\npretty easy to see, it's above the top red line.\n\nSomething I have learnt whilst studying engulfs and I have to be honest here, it was by far the most enjoyable P.A concept to learn for me so far, is where are we engulfing in to???? If we take a look on the 4hr chart this will probably answer the question as to whether this was a decent engulf or not. The 4hr chart contains a beautiful FTR which price reacted to nicely, just after the engulf, so if we think about this logically a 4hr decent-looking zone against an hourly engulf, I will go with the 4hr zone, I would even go as far to say this was a perfect FO.\n\nScott, I may be wrong here buddy, but this is what I saw on your charts.\n\nDT\n\nEdit: I just noticed where the DP was in relation to the 4hr FTR, the 4hr level could have been a target for your DP trade, well done Scott.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#312","p":13,"im":["b3b48eedd25d39570ed443dcec6b44c119b7e98c","7dd425416d204a130d276b6f52073b1df9146433"],"m":312},{"id":"flaglimits_p13_313","t":"Sharky","a":"—","d":"","n":"#313","p":13,"im":[],"m":313},{"id":"flaglimits_p13_314","t":"Aaron\n\nMorning all,\n\nA quick FL example whilst looking for QMs\n\n1707\n\nCheers all\n\nDT","a":"—","d":"","n":"#314","p":13,"im":["2628f9344849594a15a6bd4e309a89eb7f40b774","6990cd046c8d66e32ad96b0e46f737ffe39a15b5"],"m":314},{"id":"flagli